---
description: Apply DSKIT's shared implementation, skeptic review, and closure workflow.
alwaysApply: true
---

Read root AGENTS.md (and nearest package instructions). For implementation,
review, or wrap work, load docs/skills/implementation-workflow.md and follow its
TDD/review/wrap routing. Read docs/RE-ENTRY.md (one screen) and only the lane note
children/<child>/docs/RE-ENTRY.md for current scope and dependencies; never
docs/archive/ at session start. /wrap rewrites the lane note whole (80 lines at
most) and moves the replaced note to docs/archive/re-entry/<lane>.md.

On a resumed branch, fetch and consult current origin/main workflow, skeptic,
and wrap instructions before continuing. Preserve task-specific approvals,
contracts, execution restrictions, and unmerged work. Do not treat an earlier
partial ReviewExit as whole-branch approval.

One bounded result; focused evidence; complete defect-family correction;
two independent lenses; zero unresolved in-scope Critical/Major for closure;
record minors, verify the locked candidate, and finish authorized delivery.
